  ('h3', "4. Hyperinflation: a matter worth monitoring"),
  ('p', "IAS 29 includes indicators for assessing whether an economy is hyperinflationary, including a cumulative three-year inflation rate approaching or exceeding 100%. As annual inflation eases, assessing these indicators remains a matter of judgement that deserves close monitoring, particularly for subsidiaries of foreign groups reporting under IFRS, which may be asked for such analyses by their parent company or its auditors."),
